2024-10-03T06:20:57.331Z [info]: Updated item {
  "item": {
    "_id": "66794dd3d1580c3ed5330302",
    "title_en": "Publication of Tamil books",
    "description_en": "From the time Tamil originated to the present day, and in the future, to collect and preserve Tamil books, weekly and monthly magazines, from ancient palm leaf manuscripts to today's printed books, audio and video tapes, microfilms, and future digital publications. To gather and safeguard not only Tamil books but also books in other languages about Tamil and Tamilians. To collect books written by Tamilians in other languages. To create a library that encompasses all Tamil books in their entirety. To strive for the development of the Tamil language, Tamil grammar, and Tamil literature. To widely extend the use, sharing, and preservation of these across modern Tamil Nadu and the Tamil-speaking world.",
    "imageTitle_en": "3rd Tamil Festival of the Assembly",
    "image": "image-1727936457313.jpeg",
    "isDisabled": true
  }
}
2024-10-03T06:20:57.345Z [info]: Retrieved all CMS items 
2024-10-03T06:21:12.966Z [info]: Updated item {
  "item": {
    "_id": "66794e0dd1580c3ed5330304",
    "title_en": "Aid in the promotion of education",
    "description_en": "The World Tamil Sangam is an organization that plays a significant role in the development of the Tamil language and the advancement of education. It undertakes educational and cultural activities that benefit Tamil-speaking people worldwide. It promotes ancient, medieval, and modern Tamil literature globally. It organizes Tamil book fairs, literary festivals, and international Tamil conferences. It provides education of international standards to Tamil students and offers scholarships to deserving poor students.",
    "imageTitle_en": "3rd Tamil Festival of the Assembly",
    "image": "image-1727936472908.jpeg",
    "isDisabled": true
  }
}
2024-10-03T06:21:12.982Z [info]: Retrieved all CMS items 
2024-10-03T06:21:32.825Z [info]: Updated item {
  "item": {
    "_id": "66794e49d1580c3ed5330306",
    "title_en": "Erecting a statue for those who have contributed to the Tamil cause",
    "description_en": "The World Tamil Siragam is engaged in the task of erecting statues of significant individuals who have contributed to the glory of the Tamil language and the development of Tamil people. The aim is to honor these great figures of Tamil and to showcase their achievements to the current generation. Statues of prominent Tamil poets, artists, and social reformers are installed in public places. This initiative introduces the youth to their accomplishments. Statues of those who have contributed to the advancement of Tamil are also installed in Tamil schools, colleges, and universities. Through this, the Tamil community living abroad is reminded of their heritage and pride.",
    "imageTitle_en": "3rd Tamil Festival of the Assembly",
    "image": "image-1727936492812.jpeg",
    "isDisabled": true
  }
}
2024-10-03T06:21:32.840Z [info]: Retrieved all CMS items 
2024-10-03T06:21:47.115Z [info]: Updated item {
  "item": {
    "_id": "667e82a9498de3d41e9509d0",
    "title_en": "Conducting Tamil research conferences with Tamil scholars",
    "description_en": "One of the significant activities of the World Tamil Sangam is organizing Tamil research conferences with Tamil scholars. This serves as a platform for sharing precise, profound, and new information among Tamil scholars, educators, researchers, and students worldwide, and for advancing Tamil language and cultural studies. Various research works, journals, and books are published with contributions from Tamil scholars. Conferences and discussions are conducted. Through these gatherings, students and researchers can enhance their scientific and academic skills. These conferences are of great benefit to Tamil-speaking communities.",
    "imageTitle_en": "3rd Tamil Festival of the Assembly",
    "image": "image-1727936507098.jpeg",
    "isDisabled": true
  }
}
