2024-10-03T06:23:02.326Z [info]: Updated item {
  "item": {
    "_id": "66794ea1d1580c3ed5330308",
    "title_en": "Publication of Tamil books",
    "description_en": "Collecting and preserving Tamil books that have existed from ancient times to the present, as well as those that will be published in the future. This includes weekly and monthly magazines, palm leaf manuscripts, today's printed books, audio and video tapes, microfilms, future digital books, and related materials. In addition to Tamil books, collecting books in other languages about Tamil and Tamilians. Compiling books written by Tamilians in other languages. Creating a comprehensive library that contains all Tamil books. Working towards the development of the Tamil language, Tamil grammar, and literature. Broadly encompassing the use, sharing, and preservation of these across modern Tamil Nadu and the Tamil-speaking world.",
    "image": "image-1727936582266.jpeg",
    "isDisabled": true
  }
}
2024-10-03T06:23:02.339Z [info]: Retrieved all CMS items 
2024-10-03T06:23:13.744Z [info]: Updated item {
  "item": {
    "_id": "66794edad1580c3ed533030a",
    "title_en": "A statue for those who served Tamil",
    "description_en": "The World Tamil Center is engaged in the task of honoring significant individuals who have contributed to the advancement of the Tamil language and the progress of Tamil people by erecting statues in their honor. The purpose is to commemorate the greatness of these individuals and to showcase their achievements to the current generation. This involves installing statues of prominent Tamil poets, artists, and social reformers in public places. By doing so, the accomplishments of these figures are introduced to the youth. Statues of those who have contributed to the development of Tamil are also placed in Tamil schools, colleges, and universities. This effort serves to remind Tamil people living abroad of their heritage and pride.",
    "image": "image-1727936593721.jpeg",
    "isDisabled": true
  }
}
2024-10-03T06:23:13.777Z [info]: Retrieved all CMS items 
2024-10-03T06:23:48.783Z [info]: Updated item {
  "item": {
    "_id": "66794f47d1580c3ed533030c",
    "title_en": "Tamils ​​and Tamils ​​performing arts",
    "description_en": "In Tamil culture, art performances hold a significant place. These performances reflect the lifestyle, spirituality, society, and emotions of the Tamil people across various domains. There are many types of Tamil art performances, some of which include: Dramatic Arts: Theru Koothu: This is a traditional form of street drama in Tamil Nadu, popular in villages. It often depicts stories of gods like Perumal and Shiva through drama. Villupattu: This ancient art form involves singing songs while striking the bowstring. Musical Arts: Karagattam: This performance involves dancers balancing pots on their heads while paying homage to the deity. Paari Songs: These musical performances are common during temple festivals and village fairs. Dance Arts: Bharatanatyam: A classical dance form of Tamil Nadu, traditionally performed in temples and at festivals. Koothu Performances: Various types of Koothu, a folk dance-drama, are performed widely in villages, especially during village events. Traditional Dance with Props: Horse Dance: Dancers wear a dummy horse and perform as if they are riding it. This traditional dance is an important part of Tamil art performances and is popular in many parts of Tamil Nadu.",
    "image": "image-1727936628769.jpeg",
    "isDisabled": true
  }
}
