2025-07-21T10:02:42.335Z [info]: Deleted item {
  "item": {
    "title_en": "Art, Literature, and History Festival - Day 3 ",
    "description_en": "On the third day of the World Tamil Organization's second annual Art, Literature, and History Festival, held in Medan, Indonesia, the event took place on August 11 at the hall in Li Polonia Hotel. During the unveiling ceremony of a portrait of the great Chola king Rajendra Chola, who conquered Kadaram (modern-day northern Sumatra), Puducherry's Minister of Public Works, Honorable<strong> K. Lakshmi Narayanan</strong>, former Indian Parliament member Dr. <strong>R. Senthil</strong>, and Tamil Nadu Congress Party Vice President Mr. <strong>Rama Suganthan</strong> inaugurated the portrait. Lifetime achievement awards were also presented during the event to Indian and Indonesian Tamils who have worked for the well-being of their communities: Justice <strong>Janarthanam</strong> (Chennai) received the \"Sennappothar\" Award (a title for Thiruvalluvar). Mr.<strong> Marimuthu Srinivasan</strong> (Indonesia) was honored with the \"Kadaram Kondan\" Award. These awards brought great pride to the World Tamil Organization. Additionally, a collection of research papers, compiled by Dr. <strong>A. Manavazagan</strong> (Associate Professor, International Institute of Tamil Studies, Chennai) from various Tamil scholars, was released by Puducherry's Minister of Public Works, Honorable <strong>K. Lakshmi Narayanan</strong>. This compilation has been carefully curated as a must-have book for every Tamil household. During the event, Selvi<strong> Poonguzhali Purushothaman's</strong> Tamil music concert featured renditions of songs celebrating Rajendra Chola's heroic deeds along with other Tamil musical pieces. The book \"Gnaalam,\" written by <strong>Tamilmagan</strong>, was also introduced to the Tamil community in attendance.",
    "date_en": "2024-08-11",
    "image": "image-1741935786404.jpeg",
    "video": [
      "video-1741935786392.mp4"
    ],
    "gallery_images": [
      "gallery_images-1741935786366.jpeg",
      "gallery_images-1741935786372.jpeg",
      "gallery_images-1741935786374.jpeg",
      "gallery_images-1741935786376.jpeg",
      "gallery_images-1741935786378.jpeg",
      "gallery_images-1741935786381.jpeg",
      "gallery_images-1741935786384.jpeg",
      "gallery_images-1741935786387.jpeg",
      "gallery_images-1741935786389.jpeg",
      "gallery_images-1741935786390.jpeg"
    ],
    "isDisabled": true
  }
}
2025-07-21T10:02:46.026Z [info]: Deleted item {
  "item": {
    "title_en": "Art, Literature, and History Festival - Day 2",
    "description_en": "On the second day of the World Tamil Siragam's second annual Arts, Literature, and History Festival, held in Medan, Indonesia, an event took place on August 10 at the Arulmigu Raja Rajeswari Amman Temple, a temple built and managed by Tamils in the city of Padang Sidempuan. The temple complex houses a Murugan statue, which is said to be the third tallest statue of its kind in the world. Given its popularity among Tamil visitors, it was decided to place a statue of the great Tamil poet Thiruvalluvar there.At the festival on the temple grounds, Mr.<strong> K. Aravaazhi</strong>'s book <strong>\"Tamil Valartha Ulagap Perumakkal\"</strong> (The Global Dignitaries Who Nurtured Tamil) was launched by former Member of Parliament, Hon. <strong>S.R. Parthiban</strong>. Additionally, in the presence of former Indian MP Dr. <strong>R. Senthil</strong> and Tamil Nadu Congress Vice President Mr. <strong>Ram. Sugandhan</strong>, the President of World Tamil Siragam, Pattarasar <strong>K. Bharathidasan</strong>, Secretary-General Dr. <strong>M. Ponnusamy</strong>, and the festival's organizing committee chair Mr.<strong> P. Purushothaman</strong>, along with Puducherry Public Works Minister Hon. <strong>K. Lakshmi Narayanan</strong> and former Indian MP Hon. <strong>S.R. Parthiban</strong>, inaugurated Indonesia's first Thiruvalluvar statue. Thanks were extended to <strong>Siddhar Thiruthanikachalam</strong>, who donated the Thiruvalluvar statue, recognizing his remarkable service to Tamil beyond borders.Distinguished guests and Tamil scholars in attendance delivered special addresses on various topics. The festival featured a Thirumurai musical concert led by Kalaimamani Dr. Sivaraman from Puducherry, which was described as a novel experience for the Tamils of Indonesia.",
    "date_en": "2024-08-10",
    "image": "image-1741936057223.jpeg",
    "video": [
      "video-1741936056933.mp4"
    ],
    "gallery_images": [
